H2655.strongs:
Origin: from 2654;
Meaning: pleased with
KJV renders: delight in, desire, favour, please, have pleasure, whosoever would, willing, wish.

H2656.strongs:
Origin: from 2654;
Meaning: pleasure; hence (abstractly) desire; concretely, a valuable thing; hence (by extension) a matter (as something in mind)
KJV renders: acceptable, delight(-some), desire, things desired, matter, pleasant(-ure), purpose, willingly.

H2657.strongs:
Origin: from 2656 with suffixes; my delight (is) in her;
Meaning: Cheptsi-bah, a fanciful name for Palestine
KJV renders: Hephzi-bah.

H2658.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: properly, to pry into; by implication, to delve, to explore
KJV renders: dig, paw, search out, seek.

H2659.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root (perhaps rather the same as 2658 through the idea of detection);
Meaning: to blush; figuratively, to be ashamed, disappointed; causatively, to shame, reproach
KJV renders: be ashamed, be confounded, be brought to confusion (unto shame), come (be put to) shame, bring reproach.

H2660.strongs:
Origin: from 2658 or 2659; a pit of shame;
Meaning: Chepher, a place in Palestine; also the name of three Israelites
