Meaning: Chatsor, the name (thus simply) of two places in Palestine and of one in Arabia
KJV renders: Hazor.

H2675.strongs:
Origin: from 2674 and a Aramaizing form of the feminine of 2319 (compare 2323);
Meaning: new Chatsor, a place in Palestine
KJV renders: Hazor, Hadattah (as if two places).

H2676.strongs:
Origin: from 2673;
Meaning: the middle (of the night)
KJV renders: mid(-night).

H2677.strongs:
Origin: from 2673;
Meaning: the half or middle
KJV renders: half, middle, mid(-night), midst, part, two parts.

H2678.strongs:
Origin: or חֵצִי; prolongation from 2671;
Meaning: an arrow
KJV renders: arrow.

H2679.strongs:
Origin: from 2677 and the plural of 4496, with the article interposed; midst of the resting-places;
Meaning: Chatsi-ham-Menuchoth, an Israelite
KJV renders: half of the Manahethites.

H2680.strongs:
Origin: patronymically from 2679;
Meaning: a Chatsi-ham-Menachtite or descendant of Chatsi-ham-Menuchoth
KJV renders: half of the Manahethites.

H2681.strongs:
Origin: a collateral form of 2691;
Meaning: a court or abode
