H2762.strongs:
Origin: from 2760;
Meaning: properly, a net, i.e. (by analogy) lattice
KJV renders: lattice.

H2763.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to seclude; specifically (by a ban) to devote to religious uses (especially destruction); physical and reflexive, to be blunt as to the nose
KJV renders: make accursed, consecrate, (utterly) destroy, devote, forfeit, have a flat nose, utterly (slay, make away).

H2764.strongs:
Origin: or (Zechariah 14:11) חֶרֶם; from 2763;
Meaning: physical (as shutting in) a net (either literally or figuratively); usually a doomed object; abstractly extermination
KJV renders: (ac-) curse(-d, -d thing), dedicated thing, things which should have been utterly destroyed, (appointed to) utter destruction, devoted (thing), net.

H2765.strongs:
Origin: from 2763; devoted;
Meaning: Chorem, a place in Palestine
KJV renders: Horem.

H2766.strongs:
Origin: from 2763; snub-nosed;
Meaning: Charim, an Israelite
KJV renders: Harim.

H2767.strongs:
Origin: from 2763; devoted;
Meaning: Chormah, a place in Palestine
KJV renders: Hormah.

H2768.strongs:
Origin: from 2763; abrupt;
Meaning: Chermon, a mount of Palestine
KJV renders: Hermon.

H2769.strongs:
Origin: plural of 2768;
Meaning: Hermons, i.e. its peaks
KJV renders: the Hermonites.

H2770.strongs:
Origin: from 2763;
Meaning: a sickle (as cutting)
KJV renders: sickle.

H2771.strongs:
Origin: from 2787; parched;
Meaning: Charan, the name of a man and also of a place
KJV renders: Haran.

H2772.strongs:
Origin: patrial from 2773;
Meaning: a Choronite or inhabitant of Choronaim
KJV renders: Horonite.

H2773.strongs:
Origin: dual of a derivative from 2356; double cave-town;
Meaning: Choronajim, a place in Moab
KJV renders: Horonaim.

H2774.strongs:
Origin: of uncertain derivation;
Meaning: Charnepher, an Israelite
KJV renders: Harnepher.

H2776.strongs:
Origin: the same as 2775; shining;
Meaning: Cheres, a mountain in Palestine
KJV renders: Heres.

H2777.strongs:
Origin: from 2775 (apparently in the sense of a red tile used for scraping);
Meaning: a potsherd, i.e. (by implication) a pottery; the name of a gate at Jerusalem
KJV renders: east.

H2779.strongs:
Origin: from 2778;
Meaning: properly, the crop gathered, i.e. (by implication) the autumn (and winter) season; figuratively, ripeness of age
KJV renders: cold, winter (-house), youth.

H2780.strongs:
Origin: from 2778; reproachful;
Meaning: Chareph, an Israelite
KJV renders: Hareph.

H2781.strongs:
Origin: from 2778;
Meaning: contumely, disgrace, the pudenda
KJV renders: rebuke, reproach(-fully), shame.

H2782.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: properly, to point sharply, i.e. (literally) to wound; figuratively, to be alert, to decide
KJV renders: bestir self, decide, decree, determine, maim, move.

H2783.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) from a root corresponding to 2782 in the sense of vigor;
Meaning: the loin (as the seat of strength)
KJV renders: loin.

H2784.strongs:
Origin: of uncertain derivation;
Meaning: a fetter; figuratively, a pain
KJV renders: band.

H2785.strongs:
Origin: from 2782;
Meaning: a sour grape (as sharp in taste)
KJV renders: kernel.

H2786.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to grate the teeth
KJV renders: gnash.

H2787.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to glow, i.e. literally (to melt, burn, dry up) or figuratively (to show or incite passion)
KJV renders: be angry, burn, dry, kindle.

H2788.strongs:
Origin: from 2787;
Meaning: arid
KJV renders: parched place.

H2789.strongs:
Origin: a collateral form mediating between 2775 and 2791;
Meaning: a piece of pottery
KJV renders: earth(-en), (pot-) sherd, stone.

H2790.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to scratch, i.e. (by implication) to engrave, plough; hence (from the use of tools) to fabricate (of any material); figuratively, to devise (in a bad sense); hence (from the idea of secrecy) to be silent, to let alone; hence (by implication) to be deaf (as an accompaniment of dumbness)
KJV renders: × altogether, cease, conceal, be deaf, devise, ear, graven, imagine, leave off speaking, hold peace, plow(-er, man), be quiet, rest, practise secretly, keep silence, be silent, speak not a word, be still, hold tongue, worker.

H2791.strongs:
Origin: from 2790;
Meaning: magical craft; also silence
KJV renders: cunning, secretly.

H2793.strongs:
Origin: from 2790;
Meaning: a forest (perhaps as furnishing the material for fabric)
KJV renders: bough, forest, shroud, wood.

H2794.strongs:
Origin: active participle of 2790;
Meaning: a fabricator or mechanic
KJV renders: artificer.

H2795.strongs:
Origin: from 2790;
Meaning: deaf (whether literally or spiritual)
KJV renders: deaf.

H2796.strongs:
Origin: from 2790;
Meaning: a fabricator or any material
KJV renders: artificer, ( ) carpenter, craftsman, engraver, maker, mason, skilful, ( ) smith, worker, workman, such as wrought.

H2797.strongs:
Origin: from 2792; magician;
Meaning: Charsha, one of the Nethinim
KJV renders: Harsha.

H2798.strongs:
Origin: plural of 2796;
Meaning: mechanics, the name of a valley in Jerusalem
KJV renders: Charashim, craftsmen.

H2799.strongs:
Origin: from 2790;
Meaning: mechanical work
KJV renders: carving, cutting.
